                    Design: We fine-tune a pretrained                           
                    ResNet34 on the skin lesion dataset to                      
                    classify malignant versus benign                            
                    lesions, mapping “malignant” to 1 and                       
                    others to 0. We split the data 80/20 in                     
                    a stratified manner, apply data                             
                    augmentations during training and                           
                    center cropping during validation, and                      
                    train for 5 epochs with AdamW and                           
                    BCEWithLogitsLoss. After training, we                       
                    compute the ROC AUC on the hold-out                         
                    validation set, print it, and save the                      
                    model weights. We also provide a                            
                    `predict(folder_path)` function to load                     
                    the saved model and return malignancy                       
                    probabilities for new images.                               
